        "original_id": "b73235c8-595a-5abd-8f7f-fabaee99538a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shia LaBeouf, Christopher Beau Landon, D. J. Caruso, Carl Ellsworth, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, Carrie-Anne Moss, Michael Landon\n- Works: Disturbia, Even Stevens, Paranormal Activity films\n- Awards: Young Artist Award, Daytime Emmy Award\n- Topics: acting, screenwriting, directing, filmmaking\n\nFacts:\n- Shia LaBeouf was born on June 11, 1986 and is an American actor, performance artist, and filmmaker.\n- Christopher Beau Landon was born on February 27, 1975 and is an American film director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- In 2001, Shia LaBeouf received a Young Artist Award nomination for playing Louis Stevens in the Disney Channel series Even Stevens.\n- In 2003, Shia LaBeouf won a Daytime Emmy Award for his role as Louis Stevens in Even Stevens.\n- Disturbia is a 2007 American horror thriller film directed by D. J. Caruso, written by Christopher Landon and Carl Ellsworth, and starring Shia LaBeouf, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, and Carrie-Anne Moss.\n- Christopher Beau Landon is best known as the writer of the 2007 film Disturbia and the last three Paranormal Activity films, and as the son of late actor Michael Landon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
